With iOS 27.2 and iPadOS 27.2, Apple extended <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-tv/">Apple TV</a> app profiles to the iOS version of the app.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/ios-27-2-tv-app-profiles.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1065602" /><br/>
Apple brought &zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj; profiles to tvOS <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/11/07/tvos-26-2-apple-tv-profile-update/">with tvOS 26.2</a>, but the feature has been limited to the &zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj; until now.<br/>
<br/>
&zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj; app users can create new profiles in the account settings section, which can also be used to swap between profiles. Profiles only require a name, profile rating, and information about whether the user is a child.<br/>
<br/>
Creating an account for a child limits content to a PG rating by default, but there is a customize option for more granular control. Users can select age ratings for TV shows and movies that are appropriate for the child based on their age<br/>
<br/>
